==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3.33~30 seconds<sup>100f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 10~40 seconds<sup>300f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Le'boin]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07~1 second<sup>2f~30f</sup>.
**20 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Start the [[Battle|battle]] off by sending out [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cats]] to stall the enemies and upgrade your [[Worker Cat]].

No [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]] or purchasable [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] can outrange Le'boin, so the only attacker that is safe to use is [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]], who even at level 1 can survive a hit without getting knocked back.  At '''level 6''', Titan Cat gains enough health to endure two slams of Le'boin's trunk, and at '''level 10''' he can withstand three!

The abundance of Those Guys makes it extremely difficult to reach Le'boin. The best strategy is to lure Le'boin close to the [[Cat Base]], allow 9 of Those Guys (the maximum amount that can be present at any one time in this stage) to stack up on your [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cats]], and use either [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]] or the [[Cat Cannon]] to wipe them all out at once, thereby making Le'boin open to attack. During Le'boin's downtime, you can try to time a [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]] to deal some good damage to him before he attacks again. Rinse and repeat until Le'boin succumbs to your Cows and Titans.

